  "closed_findings": [
    "Standalone dataset-series one-minute deadline now encloses initial metadata, native work and final authority, and expires before native admission after delayed metadata",
    "Empty and successful selections recheck live context even without an attached report recorder",
    "Dataset overlays retain fixed authority fields from the exact successful private query snapshot and recheck after the final annotation read",
    "Explicit microsecond windows use the same effective origin for dataset and run-side calculations while retaining requested bounds and actual run start; native worker cast proof admits only the unique UTC microsecond cast",
    "Strict retained receipt verification exposed a genuine v1 digest round-trip bug for no-rejection normalization. Result digests now canonicalize only v1 zero-length omitted output collections; publication and retained read use the same digest function. Version0 historical shape is unchanged; invalid v1 receipts have no compatibility acceptance.",
    "Old worker fixture now carries coherent producer statistics while retaining per-measure population refusal; upload completion uses the same bounded preflight as durable metadata update, preserving physical-close/cleanup proof when metadata cannot fit."
  ],
  "checked_constraints": [
    "Complete effective query key includes identity, filters, window, aggregation, mapping version, dataset revision, manifest digest and catalog version",
    "Private snapshots deeply clone manifests, mappings and dimensions before staging; duplicate same-dataset sides still charge two private artifact copies",
    "Publication checks complete child descriptor population, then parent copied byte counts and SHA256 before durable manifest publication",
    "Artifact reports have at most two admitted rows and describe object selection/staging bytes without physical DuckDB scan claims",
    "Legacy no-manifest populations scan every owned artifact; current attempts require fresh manifest; legacy input/result digest bytes and immutable replay receipts remain compatible",
    "Empty selections still require available native capability and live authority; malformed or future manifests fail before artifact IO",
    "Worker protocol v3 bounds, output summaries and series casts remain typed, bounded and operation scoped",
    "Precision cases cover positive and pre-epoch instants, nanosecond offsets, non-UTC queries, collapsed native windows, missing samples and whole-publication rate safety",
    "Native acceptance fixtures exercise real multi-file import, distinct same-dataset side filters, missing rows, percentile/rate equivalence, excluded object removal and selected artifact corruption",
    "Actual PostgreSQL test fixture owns and verifies removal of only its unique schema; metadata-only publication tests explicitly label synthetic proof",
    "After the retained four-file upload-proof review, only one additional production storage function changed: v1 result digest zero-field normalization. The original strict manifest/receipt and generic metadata writer guards remain intact.",
    "New two-store SQLite/actual PostgreSQL fixtures independently read receipts, associate a real same-project run, preserve proof through deleting/deleted retries, refuse stale or manifest-changing generic saves, retain historical receipt results, close/reopen, and test cancel/fail/new-owner retries. These fixtures qualify metadata authority; they do not invent OS quiescence.",
    "Root corrected only the whole-publication rate test: invalid merged rates remain nil; an independent average assertion proves preserved count2 and unchanged source timestamp/window.",
    "Artifact byte reporting is selected/staged/avoided object data, not physical DuckDB operator scan metrics; approved query reports remain bounded to two plans."
  ],
